# Frostpeak: snow, ice, a hermit's small fire, and the Watcher, a giant
# of stone holding the peak's ember.

place the peak
  title: Frostpeak
  the sky: grey
  the mist: light
  the ground: snow, 50 by 50 m
  you come in at 0 19, facing 0

  a stone giant called the Watcher at 0 -11, unlit
  an ember stone at 0 -8.4
  a tent at 9 6, turned -60
  a campfire at 6.4 7.4
  Ysolde at 5.4 9.2, facing 210

  a way to the ford at 0 22, turned 180
  a way to the hill at -18 -8, turned 70

  10 ice spires around 0 -4, 14 to 19 m away
  9 snow rocks between -20 -20 and 20 20
  6 standing stones in a line from -9 -3 to 9 -3

  when you first arrive
    say: The path up from the river is steep and icy. At the top the wind drops to nothing, and the snow is very quiet.
    say: In the middle of the peak sits a giant of stone with its knees drawn up. Beside a small tent, someone has kept a fire going.

  when you talk to Ysolde
    if met ysolde
      Ysolde: Ring the bell, if you have one. The Watcher only wakes for something true.
    otherwise
      remember met ysolde
      Ysolde: Ha! A climber. Sit by my fire. It's small, but it's mine, and the Grey doesn't like it.
      Ysolde: You've come for the Watcher's ember, haven't you? It asks one riddle. Everyone gets it wrong.
      choose
        choice: Will you tell me the answer?
          Ysolde: If I knew it, I'd have the ember. But I'll tell you what twenty years alone up here taught me. A fire kept to yourself is a lonely thing.
        choice: Why do you live up here alone?
          Ysolde: I came up to keep my fire safe from everyone. Twenty years. I've had a long time to wonder whether that was clever.
          Ysolde: Thank you for asking. Nobody has asked me anything in a very long time.
          add 1 to kindness

  when you look at the Watcher
    say: A giant of stone. Snow has piled on its shoulders for a hundred years. In front of it, on a block of stone, something burns as white as a star.

  when you look at the ember stone
    if the watcher gave its ember
      say: The block of stone is empty, and the snow around it has melted into a perfect circle.
    otherwise
      say: The peak's ember, on a block of dark stone. When you reach for it, the air turns so cold your fingers ache. It isn't yours to take. Not yet.

  when you talk to the Watcher
    if the watcher gave its ember
      The Watcher: GO WELL, LITTLE FIRE.
    otherwise if you have the silver bell
      say: You hold up the silver bell and ring it. The note is tiny, but the whole mountain seems to hear it.
      light the Watcher
      say: Snow slides off the giant's shoulders. Two eyes open, cold and blue.
      The Watcher: WHO RINGS THE RIVER'S BELL? ANSWER ME, AND THE EMBER IS YOURS.
      The Watcher: WHAT GROWS WHEN YOU SHARE IT, AND DIES WHEN YOU KEEP IT?
      choose
        choice: Gold.
          The Watcher: GOLD KEPT IS STILL GOLD. NO.
          put out the Watcher
          say: The eyes close. Snow starts to settle again. You can ring the bell again when you are ready.
        choice: A secret.
          The Watcher: A SECRET SHARED IS A SECRET LOST. NO.
          put out the Watcher
          say: The eyes close. Snow starts to settle again. You can ring the bell again when you are ready.
        choice: Fire.
          The Watcher: FIRE. SHARE IT, THEN.
          say: The block of stone cracks open with a sound like a bell. The ember rolls free, and snow melts in a circle around your feet.
          you get the peak ember
          add 1 to embers
          hide the ember stone
          remember the watcher gave its ember
        choice if met ysolde: Fire. Kept alone, it's lonely. Shared, it can light a whole village.
          The Watcher: THE HERMIT HAS TAUGHT YOU WELL. OR YOU HAVE TAUGHT HER. SHARE IT, THEN.
          say: The block of stone cracks open with a sound like a bell. The ember rolls free, and snow melts in a circle around your feet.
          you get the peak ember
          add 1 to embers
          add 1 to kindness
          hide the ember stone
          remember the watcher gave its ember
    otherwise
      say: You shout. You knock on the cold stone. The Watcher doesn't stir. It's waiting for some other kind of call.

  when you leave for the hill
    if embers is 0
      say: The long path down to the Hearth hill. You've nothing to bring the Hearth yet.
    otherwise
      say: You follow the long path down the mountain's far side. Below, in the dark, the Hearth hill waits.
      go to the hill
